WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.870
I thought this was a really cool part of
your journal

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:08.160
that you wrote and you're talking about
getting through that kind of stuff so

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:13.500
here we go back to the journal it is
easy to be motivated to succeed in the

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:19.020
beginning of an endeavor and when you
are close to the end the most difficult

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:24.689
part and the part where people quit is
when they are in the thick of it and it

00:00:24.689 --> 00:00:28.830
is unclear whether they have the
strength and stamina to make it the rest

00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:33.870
of the way while I never actually
doubted my ability to walk again during

00:00:33.870 --> 00:00:40.020
my recovery I am certainly subject to
the inner monologue rationalizing why it

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:44.370
is okay to quit or to not push myself to
the goal that I have written down on

00:00:44.370 --> 00:00:51.899
paper one way I have recognized to aid
in shutting that monologue the fuck up

00:00:51.899 --> 00:01:00.210
is celebrating milestones the hardest
part of working toward a goal is when we

00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:04.229
are either making slow progress or
negative progress and having the

00:01:04.229 --> 00:01:08.310
patience and confidence to know that the
improvements we make over the long

00:01:08.310 --> 00:01:14.939
periods as opposed to the short periods
are what matter milestones are what

00:01:14.939 --> 00:01:20.270
remind us that we are making progress
even if it isn't apparent every day in

00:01:20.270 --> 00:01:25.259
rowing I've heard of people that count
strokes until the finish line using sets

00:01:25.259 --> 00:01:33.659
of 10 personally I like to count to 50s
for making up a race when I ran the

00:01:33.659 --> 00:01:38.189
nation's triathlon I picked points ahead
of me to make it to and when I got there

00:01:38.189 --> 00:01:44.100
I'd pick a new point anything we can use
to keep our minds from succumbing to the

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:51.030
monologue will work not only ensure
short-term goals but also in long-term

00:01:51.030 --> 00:01:59.040
goals like graduating from college or
learning to use prosthetics great advice

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:03.229
for anybody to pay attention to

